---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Legal from '../components/Legal.astro';
---
<Base title="Terms | JP Silva Digital"
      description="How JP Silva Digital projects work: scope, revisions, ownership, and what is guaranteed.">
  <Legal heading="Terms" updated="July 2026">
    <div class="note">
      <span class="lbl">What this page is</span>
      <p class="small">A plain-English summary of how projects run, not the contract itself.
      The agreement you actually sign is the written proposal for your project, and it governs
      if the two ever differ.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="h3">Ownership and handover</h2>
    <p class="body">You own the completed website you pay for. The domain, the content, the
    source code and the analytics are yours, registered in your name. There is no licence, no
    lease, and no platform fee.</p>
    <p class="body">After launch you choose how the site is run. I can continue hosting and
    looking after it under an agreed scope, or the project is handed over to you with the
    access and documentation you need &mdash; website and hosting access, the project
    repository, domain instructions, and the details of any third-party services it depends
    on. The exact list varies with what the project uses. Ongoing care is never a condition of
    the build, and if you leave nothing is held back.</p>
    <p class="body">The free homepage demo is a concept shown privately so you can decide
    whether to go ahead. It is not a finished website and it does not transfer ownership of
    one.</p>

    <h2 class="h3">Ongoing care</h2>
    <p class="body">Where you choose it, Website Care covers hosting and deployment, keeping
    the site running, backups, monitoring and technical support within the scope agreed in
    writing. Website Care with Content Updates adds a set number of small content changes each
    month: replacing a photo, changing a paragraph, updating hours or a phone number, editing
    an existing service description, or changing an existing button or link. New pages, new
    functionality, new integrations and full copy rewrites are project work, quoted separately.
    No care level includes unlimited changes.</p>

    <h2 class="h3">Scope and revisions</h2>
    <p class="body">Every project starts with a written scope. Revision rounds are named in
    the proposal — one with Starter, two with Business Growth, project-specific on Custom.
    Work outside the agreed scope is quoted separately before it starts, never billed after.</p>

    <h2 class="h3">Schedule</h2>
    <p class="body">A launch date is agreed in writing before work begins. If it slips for
    reasons on my side, the remedy is stated in your proposal. If it slips because content or
    approvals are outstanding, the date moves by agreement.</p>

    <h2 class="h3">What is guaranteed</h2>
    <p class="body">Scope, price and launch date. <strong>Not</strong> search rankings, lead
    volume, or revenue — no honest supplier can promise those, and any who do are describing
    something other than what they will deliver.</p>

    <h2 class="h3">Payment</h2>
    <p class="body">Every project is quoted after a conversation, and the price, the payment
    schedule and any deposit are set out in the written proposal before work starts. There are
    no charges that are not in that document, and the free demo and the consultation are free
    with nothing attached to either.</p>
  </Legal>
</Base>
